    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0599" n="1433" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/261</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-29T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7073. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 260. Your 347, Embassy’s 9240, March 27, 6 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Borneo</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Cornelis</hi> were requisitioned
                    without due consideration having been given to their being in Panama Canal. We
                    thought it wiser to release them later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
